The default Windows 10 is a disaster and will come across as not feeling snappy! You can compare it to Ubuntu 20.04 / 20.10 on the same hardware and come out thinking wow Windows
must have something fundamentally wrong with it :-)

Fact is, they are both just as bad. But Windows does have better Device support, DirectX is bad ass! and Display Monitor support. All in all, it is a great usable desktop OS that works across a wide variety of hardware in a decently performant way.

But first here is what we need to do :

* disable security (most of it)
 - This is really the big one


* disable startup apps

* disable services (unneccesary ones)

* disable search indexing

* strip down the start setting to search nothing
  (manually add programs to the tiles)


* Disable Windows Defender
https://www.windowscentral.com/how-permanently-disable-windows-defender-windows-10


